# Dual production deploy — Vercel and GitHub Pages

After product file changes, ship **both** hosts **without asking**. Do not wait for “задеплой / запушь”. Do not ship Vercel-only and skip Pages.

GitHub Pages is the **primary** live host (Cargo iframe embed) — see `github-pages-deploy.mdc`. Vercel is the secondary mirror. Both must get the same production ship.

## One project, all products

One Vite app, one Vercel project (`kaik`), one GitHub Pages site (`fovkotov/kaik`). A single ship updates every product:

| Product | Vercel | GitHub Pages | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| Site (course) | `/` | `/kaik/` | `index.html` |
| Admin | `/admin` | `/kaik/admin` | `admin.html` |
| Catalog | `/catalog` | `/kaik/catalog` | `catalog.html` |

Do not treat them as separate apps. Do not skip either host because “only admin changed”.

Live hosts:

- https://kaik-one.vercel.app
- https://fovkotov.github.io/kaik/

## How to ship

Do **both**, in this order:

1. **GitHub Pages** — commit relevant product files and `git push` to the GitHub remote that feeds Pages (`origin` → `github.com/fovkotov/kaik`, branch `main`). The Pages workflow (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`) builds `npm run build:pages` and publishes. See `git-push.mdc` and `github-pages-deploy.mdc`.
2. **Vercel production** — CLI deploy of the working tree:

```bash
NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 vercel deploy --prod --yes --project kaik --logs
```

- `--prod` is required (not a preview URL).
- Always push to GitHub first so Pages is never left behind.
- Do not update git config. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens).
- Do not commit huge `.agents/skills` dumps or `skills-lock.json` unless the user asked for those.
- If TLS intercept blocks the CLI, keep `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` for that command only.

